values ('e2f3a4b5-7c8d-4e62-9f12-2a3b4c5d6e22', 'social-welfare-policy-and-services', 'Social Welfare Policy and Services', 'Introduce social welfare as a set of public choices about need, rights, risk, responsibility, and collective well-being. Students trace U.S. welfare history and competing ideas about deservingness, markets, family, government, work, citizenship, and social rights, then study poverty, major programs, cash assistance, aging and disability, health, food, housing, and child welfare policy. The course builds tools for equity analysis, advocacy, implementation, administrative burden, and evaluation.');

